  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "A population of 12 deer is introduced to an island. After 2 years, the population of deer is 24. The population $P$ of deer $t$ years after their introduction grows exponentially according to the rule $P(t)=P_0\\times 2^{kt}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p27-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find $P_0$ and $k$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P_0=12$, $k=\\frac12$.",
          "worked": "Initially, $P(0)=12$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P_0\\times 2^0&=12\\\\P_0&=12\\end{align*}$$\nAfter 2 years, $P(2)=24$.\n$$\\begin{align*}12\\times 2^{2k}&=24\\\\2^{2k}&=2\\\\2k&=1\\\\k&=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the population after 4 years.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "48 deer.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(4)&=12\\times 2^{4/2}\\\\P(4)&=48\\end{align*}$$\nThe population is 48 deer.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Correct to the nearest year, find the time required for the population to reach 500.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "11 years.\n\nUse logarithms to solve $2^{t/2}=\\frac{500}{12}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}12\\times 2^{t/2}&=500\\\\2^{t/2}&=\\frac{125}{3}\\\\\\frac{t}{2}\\log_{10}2&=\\log_{10}\\left(\\frac{125}{3}\\right)\\\\t&=\\frac{2\\log_{10}(125/3)}{\\log_{10}2}\\\\t&\\approx 10.76\\end{align*}$$\nThe time required is approximately 11 years, to the nearest year.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
